A||||2||87fiero_gt||Losing power V6 auto
Z||000000||87fiero_gt||07-03-99||08:58 AM||||I put in a new (remanufactured) distributor along with ign module, cap, rotor, coil, pickup coil, plugs, plug wires. I had to reset the dist from scratch and reset the timing. It starts up immediately, but now it is very sluggish, acceleration is poor. Could I have messed something up changing the plugs on the back side, goofed up the dist installation? I will be checking for vacuum leaks. Any help is appreciated.
Z||000001||batboy||07-03-99||11:58 AM||||Hopefully you have already put a timing light onto it and retimed it (must do this with any distibutor change). Double check that all the plug wires are going to the right places. Make sure all the wire connectors are securely fastened.
Z||000002||GREENDANO||07-04-99||07:04 AM||||Ground the ALDL conector terminal A to B before you check the timing.  I didn't and had my timing about 12 degrees retarded.  It was quite a dog.<br>   Dan-O
